# team-lead-skills.manifest — the coordination skill subset a *team-lead* home repo
# carries under .claude/skills/ (PROJ-039/T-038).
#
# A migrated build-agent home repo is HOOKS-ONLY (no skills/ at all). A migrated
# team LEAD additionally needs the coordination skills it actually invokes to lead
# its team — and ONLY those. This manifest names that subset; scaffold.sh and
# sync-agent-tooling.sh copy these skills (and no others) from the canonical
# agent-tooling/skills/ source into a team-lead home repo's .claude/skills/,
# byte-identical, and test_skills_parity.py enforces it (subset present + byte-
# identical + NO out-of-subset skill, e.g. session ceremony stays hook-driven).
#
# Subset = the skills a fissioned team lead invokes to LEAD (not for its own
# session-end — result authoring stays with the SessionEnd finalise hook, T-035):
#
#   consolidate-tasks   local-mode consolidation of the lead's team repo
#   launch-session      launching the lead's team agents
#   create-task         guided task-board entry creation (identity-routed, no apex hardcode)
#   usage-report        7-day usage digest, output resolved via team_repo (D-2, T-076;
#                        de-apexed — no hardcoded podzoneTeam/team/hermes path, no
#                        hardcoded ~/workspace/agent-tooling tool path)
#
# DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED (kept hook-driven / out of the parity-enforced subset):
#   session-start / session-end   — agent ceremony is hook-driven in every home repo;
#                                    the finalise hook owns the result (T-035). A team
#                                    lead does not need them as skills.
#
# Format: one canonical skill name per line (must exist as agent-tooling/skills/<name>/).
# Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.

consolidate-tasks
launch-session
create-task
usage-report
